Calc: an .xlsx import groups filled-down (shared) formula cells as they are created, not only at the end.

Every shared formula cell was created with its own copy of the token array and the cells were only grouped by
ScColumn::RegroupFormulaCells after the whole workbook was read, so at the peak of loading a sheet of filled-down
formulas held one token array per cell: a 50 MB workbook with 3.5 million formula cells held about 400 MB of copies
(1.66 GB peak heap), and a 200 MB one reached 7.9 GB while opening.

Each cell is now joined, once its cached result and recalc mode are set, to the formula cell right above it with
exactly the rule RegroupFormulaCells applies (same token comparison; the upper cell's group, or a new group of
two whose code is the upper cell's), and its copy is freed at once. Cells are created top to bottom, and
RegroupFormulaCells keeps existing groups and merges equal neighbours as before, so the final groups are the same.
New logic in sc/source/filter/inc/hstsharedformulajoin.hxx; the hook is one line in applySharedFormulas.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0); the new file is LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary.
Test: CppunitTest_sc_subsequent_filters_test4 testSharedFormulaXLSX and test2 testSharedFormulaXLSB (group top
rows and lengths after import); saved .xlsx compared part by part before/after on the large fixtures.
